{"name":"Muesli","hex":"#9e7e53","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"muesli","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A breakfast dish based on uncooked rolled oats and fruit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/muesli"}],"entries":[{"title":"Muesli","blocks":[{"text":"Muesli is a cold Swiss dish that has become a common breakfast cereal prepared without cooking. Developed around 1900 by Swiss physician Maximilian Bircher-Benner for patients in his hospital in Switzerland, it is also consumed for supper as Birchermüesli complet, 'Bircher's complete little mush', i.e., muesli with café complet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Dorset_Cereals_muesli.jpg/330px-Dorset_Cereals_muesli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muesli","wikidata":"Q52406"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Muesli.jpg/500px-Muesli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Muesli.jpg/1280px-Muesli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Muesli.jpg/500px-Muesli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A dry muesli mix served with milk and sliced fresh banana","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMuesli.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Fresh-muesli.jpg/500px-Fresh-muesli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Fresh-muesli.jpg/1280px-Fresh-muesli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Fresh-muesli.jpg/500px-Fresh-muesli.jpg?utm_source=